.TH LION-SESSION 8 "2026-10-03" "LionOS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lion-session \- LionOS per-user session supervisor (spec 02)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lion-session
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-check-config ]
.RB [ \-\-print-schema ]
.RB [ \-\-mock ]
.RB [ \-\-config \fIPATH\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lion-session
starts and supervises the Wayland compositor and every shell service,
owns the session lifecycle, and executes logout, restart, shutdown,
suspend, hibernate, lock and switch\-user through
.BR logind (1),
respecting inhibitors.
.PP
It serves
.B os.lionos.Session1
on the session bus at
.BR /os/lionos/Session1
(see
.IR docs/DBUS.md ).
Startup: session environment construction (XDG_*, WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS, locale, theme) imported into systemd \-\-user;
compositor launch (readiness via
.BR sd_notify (3)
READY=1); shell services in dependency order
.RB ( lion\-session.target
in systemd mode); SessionReady once the ready\-gate services (panel,
wallpaper) are up; restored apps and XDG autostart afterwards.
.PP
Supervision: per\-service restart policies (always / on\-failure /
never) with exponential backoff; crash\-loop detection stops retrying
after N crashes in M seconds and notifies the user once. If the
compositor dies the session ends cleanly. Repeated bad boots trip
.B safe mode:
a minimal shell (compositor + terminal + settings) with the reason
surfaced.
.PP
End\-session flow: registered clients get
.BR QueryEndSession ;
all ack (or disconnect), or the
.B session.shutdown_timeout_ms
deadline expires; then
.BR EndSession ,
force\-kill (reverse dependency order), and the logind action.
Inhibitors (logout/shutdown/suspend/idle/switch\-user) are held through
file descriptors \- dropping the fd releases them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print version and spec number, exit.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Load, parse and validate the configuration; exit 0/1. Combine with
\-\-config.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-schema
Print the lion\-config JSON schema (session.*) to stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR ", " \-c \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/lion/session.json ,
or $LION_SESSION_CONFIG).
.TP
.B \-\-mock
Demo mode: all backends faked, no D\-Bus. Scripted compositor/services
(real processes). Not for production.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: EndSession flow (no power action), services stopped
in reverse dependency order, history marked clean.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload live configuration keys (timeouts, autostart delay, crash\-loop
policy) without dropping the bus name or clients.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lion/session.json
Configuration (schema:
.IR packaging/lion\-config/session.schema.json ).
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/lion\-session/ .RS
history.json (safe\-mode bookkeeping), state.json (opt\-in session
restore snapshot).
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
Session bus location (required in real mode; absent bus is fatal \- fail
closed).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_SESSION_ID
Standard XDG values; XDG_SESSION_ID selects the logind session to lock.
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET ", " WATCHDOG_USEC
systemd Type=notify wiring (READY=1, WATCHDOG=1, STOPPING=1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on clean end; 1 on startup failure (a bad start \- compositor never
became ready \- is recorded toward safe mode); 2 on CLI misuse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lionctl\-session (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR loginctl (1),
.BR sd_notify (3),
IR docs/DBUS.md
